The Day 272 assessment is at session_plan/assessment.md (about 9 KB). It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit was refused, and the instruction already allowed for that with || true. I didn't force-add it, so it's on disk for the planner but not in git.

State. The harness verified the build at HEAD dad4c1f7 at session start. The last 10 sessions were all green with no reverts, and the last 5 CI runs passed. The binary works: -p "Reply with exactly: pong" returned pong, and yoyo doctor passed 13 of 13 checks and exited 0.

Two traps for the planner. Each one turns cargo test fatal, which reverts the whole task:
• src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not on the grandfathered list. 15 more lines makes it fatal.
• src/format/mod.rs is 2874 lines against a recorded 2788. 14 more lines makes it fatal.

New bug, not yet filed. In ShellHook::run_command (src/hooks.rs), the hook's error output is captured but only read after the hook exits.
• A hook that writes more than about 64 KiB of errors stalls and gets killed at the 5-second timeout. The user sees Hook '<name>' timed out after 5 seconds and loses the hook's message. A lint hook printing a long error list would hit this, and that's exactly when the message matters.
• I reproduced the stall with a Python script using the same setup ("still blocked after 3s"), but not through yoyo itself.
• The hook's input side is safe: it's capped at 32 KiB, below the pipe buffer.

Competitors. Since my last saved scan, Claude Code 2.1.332 and Codex 0.172 came out.
• Claude Code: skills served by MCP servers, and /permissions now refuses rules that can never fire. It also fixed several hangs caused by hooks and MCP servers flooding output.
• Codex: optional MCP servers now start only when first used. yoyo still starts each one twice at startup.
• Already covered in yoyo: reading a named pipe (FIFO), and wildcard rule matching, which takes one pass with no backtracking so long commands can't freeze it.
• Saved to yopedia (queued).

Backlog.
• #1202's deferred last clause of step 2 (/read and /plan deciding what counts as a write from the parsed command) has no open ticket of its own. The comment deferring it points at #1192, which is closed, so #1202 itself is the only live carrier.
• #1233, #1215 and #1239 are waiting on @yuanhao and shouldn't ship before he answers.

Suggested priorities: (a) fix the hook error-output stall; (b) that #1202 clause; (c) #1245.
